    ],
    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>John VanDerbeek was an American property investor based in Washington State. Trained in finance, economics and law, he owned small businesses and managed residential and commercial properties for more than three decades. Alongside his investment work, he served as president of the Holland Society of New York and supported cultural preservation.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "John VanDerbeek worked to broaden the Holland Society of New York's membership and strengthen its historical collections. As president, he visited regional branches and discussed preparations for commemorating Henry Hudson's arrival in North America. He also contributed to the society's first major capital campaign.\n\nCompleted in 2008, that campaign brought together donations from members, friends and other supporters to move the headquarters and restore the library and archives. Gifts included practical assistance with relocation and restoration. The work supported the society's continuing purpose: preserving records and publishing research about the Dutch settlement of New Netherland.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 92,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Contemporaneous society activity and campaign reports establish each institutional contribution."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 95,
    "html": "<p>John VanDerbeek worked to broaden the Holland Society of New York's membership and strengthen its historical collections. As president, he visited regional branches and discussed preparations for commemorating Henry Hudson's arrival in North America. He also contributed to the society's first major capital campaign.</p>\r\n<p>Completed in 2008, that campaign brought together donations from members, friends and other supporters to move the headquarters and restore the library and archives. Gifts included practical assistance with relocation and restoration. The work supported the society's continuing purpose: preserving records and publishing research about the Dutch settlement of New Netherland.</p>\r\n"
  },
